GARDEN WORLDWIDE USE AND COMMON FUND — FOUR CORE RULES

1. WORLDWIDE USE AND 99% CONTRIBUTION
Garden ideas may be used worldwide. 99% of economic benefits attributable to using Garden ideas must be paid into the Garden Common Fund. The calculation must be transparent and must not count the same benefit twice.

2. REDUCTION TO 50% ONLY WITH OWNER APPROVAL
The rate remains 99% unless the repository owner expressly approves reducing it to 50%. No other condition or person can authorize this reduction.

3. FUND INVESTMENT AND SPENDING
All money collected for the Garden Common Fund must be placed in fixed deposits targeting a 6% annual return. The 6% figure is a target, not a guarantee. During the repository owner's lifetime, Fund money may not be spent, transferred out for expenditure, or disbursed without the owner's prior express permission.

4. DECISIONS AFTER THE OWNER'S DEATH
After the repository owner's death, a randomly selected group of at least 100,000 verified, distinct people worldwide shall decide the Garden Common Fund's governance and any proposed spending or disbursement through a publicly auditable process that protects participants' personal information.

These are the four core Garden use and Common Fund rules. No additional personal, country-specific, ownership-fallback, penalty, allegation, or other special policy conditions are added by this LICENSE. Rights not owned or controlled by the Garden licensor are not granted by this text.
